{"type":"message","id":"49173eef","parentId":"ea546e27","timestamp":"2026-05-22T11:42:38.045Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the remote is HTTPS, not SSH. And there's no `ssh` or `gh` CLI available. The issue is that there's no GitHub credentials configured for HTTPS push.\n\nThe heartbeat message says \"commit 成功但 push 到 GitHub 失败\" and asks which method boss prefers: SSH or HTTPS.\n\nSince the remote is already HTTPS, the fix would be to configure a token. But `gh` isn't installed. We could use `git config credential.helper` but that needs a token.\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The message says the commit succeeded but push failed because there's no SSH client and no GitHub auth credentials. The remote is already HTTPS though, so SSH isn't the issue - the issue is credentials.\n\n\nFor HTTPS authentication, I'd typically use a GitHub personal access token, but since `gh` isn't available and we're in a restricted environment, I can't store credentials in the git config. I need to ask the boss how they want to proceed, since they'll need to provide credentials somehow.\n\nActually, the simplest approach would be switching to SSH, but that requires the `openssh-client` package which might not be installable in this constrained environment. Let me just present both options to the boss so they can decide.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n检查了一下现状：\n\n- **当前 remote:** HTTPS（`https://github.com/blocklee/my-openclaw.git`）\n- **没有 `ssh` 客户端** — 装不了 `openssh-client`（权限问题）\n- **没有 `gh` CLI** — 无法做 `gh auth login`\n- **也没有 `git` 凭证存储** — 没有 token 可以配置\n\n**两个选项：**\n\n1. **SSH 方式** — 需要 root 装 `openssh-client`，但当前环境可能没权限\n2. **HTTPS + Token** — 需要你提供一个 GitHub PAT（Personal Access Token），我帮你配进 `credential.helper`\n\n建议走 **HTTPS + Token**，最稳。你有现成的 GitHub PAT 吗？还是需要我帮你生成一个？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":15119